<v Ron Book>Why is it my job? It's my job because, unfortunately for me, I have a daughter who suffered at the hands of a no-good-for-nothing, no-good-for-nothing, no redeeming qualities, no redeeming social values, no redeeming humanistic values, who raped my daughter, who beat my daughter. I am the predators' and offenders' worst enemy. I am their worst nightmare, and I will be that forever until the day I die when they put me in a pine box and put me in the ground.
<v Ron Book>为什么这是我的工作？因为不幸的是，我有个女儿，她落入了一个一无是处、毫无救药、没有任何救赎价值、没有任何社交价值、没有任何人性价值的家伙手中，他强奸了我的女儿，毒打了我的女儿。我是这些捕食者和犯罪者的最大敌人。我是他们最可怕的噩梦，我会一直这样下去，直到我死的那天，他们把我装进松木盒埋入地下。

00:39:32.850 --> 00:40:08.600
<v Isaiah Thompson>Around 15 years ago, Ron Book hired a nanny who started molesting his daughter. It's an awful story. The nanny was arrested, brought to trial, and sent to prison, but that was just the beginning for Book. When he found out there was no law compelling convicted sex offenders to provide blood samples for HIV tests, he wrote one and got it passed. When the nanny started writing letters to his daughter from prison, and Book found out there was no law explicitly against it, he simply went ahead and got that law passed, too. It's now called the Lauren Book Protection Act, after his daughter.
<v Isaiah Thompson>大约15年前，罗恩·布克雇了一个保姆，开始猥亵他的女儿。那是一个可怕的故事。保姆被逮捕、受审并送进监狱，但这只是布克的开始。当他发现没有法律强制要求被定罪的性犯罪者提供血液样本进行艾滋病测试时，他起草了一项法案并获通过。当那个保姆开始从监狱写信给他女儿，而布克发现没有法律明确禁止时，他又直接推动通过了那项法律。现在以他女儿的名字命名，称为《劳伦·布克保护法》。

00:40:08.600 --> 00:40:35.350
<v Isaiah Thompson>But Book didn't stop there. He and his daughter went on a kind of tour of Florida, pushing residency restrictions. In 2005, he helped write and pass the law in Miami Dade County that required sex offenders to find housing at least 2,500 feet from any school, playground, or daycare, leaving sex offenders with very few places to live. They ended up under that bridge, homeless.
<v Isaiah Thompson>但布克并没有就此停止。他和女儿在佛罗里达州做了一次巡回演讲，推动居住限制。2005年，他帮助起草并推动迈阿密戴德县通过了那项法律，要求性犯罪者找到距离任何学校、游乐场或日托中心至少2500英尺的住房，让性犯罪者几乎无处可住。他们最终流落到那座桥下，无家可归。

00:40:35.350 --> 00:40:47.490
<v Isaiah Thompson>And the person in Miami Dade that's in charge of helping homeless people like these find homes and jobs, the person with the resources, the manpower, and a budget of $40 million to help them also happens to be Ron Book.
