00:40:47.490 --> 00:41:05.820
<v Ron Book>I am chairman of the Miami Dade County Homeless Trust. I have been the chairman of this body for 16 years. This particular population is a piece of the homeless population and I have a responsibility to find them housing and jobs. That's what my homeless trust does. And these guys are a component of that.
<v Ron Book>我是迈阿密戴德县无家可归者信托基金的主席。我已经担任该机构主席16年了。这个特定群体是无家可归者的一部分，我有责任为他们寻找住房和工作。这就是我的信托基金所做的。这些人是其中的一部分。

00:41:05.820 --> 00:41:16.310
<v Isaiah Thompson>So the one person who could possibly help the sex offenders find a place to live is their biggest enemy, the person who got them there in the first place.
<v Isaiah Thompson>所以唯一能帮助性犯罪者找到住处的人，竟然是他们最大的敌人，也就是最初把他们推到这一步的那个人。

00:41:16.310 --> 00:41:22.610
<v Isaiah Thompson>[CAR DRIVING] For as much press as this bridge has gotten, it's surprisingly hard to find.
<v Isaiah Thompson>[开车声]尽管这座桥得到了很多媒体报道，但要找到它出奇地难。

00:41:22.610 --> 00:41:29.880
<v Isaiah Thompson>We're looking out for some kind of opening in the fence here. You're going to have to-- we might miss it the first time, because we're going so fast.
